# Scalar functions take no named arguments.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, small: int, timestamp: datetime, wait: timespan, shipped: bool)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where round(amount, digits = 2) > 1
---- expected
error[DS2011]: `round` takes no named arguments
  --> query:1:41
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where round(amount, digits = 2) > 1
  |                                         ^^^^^^^^^^ named argument
  |
  = help: pass the value by position: `round(amount, 2)`
  = note: signature: `round(x: T[, digits: integer]) -> T, where T is a number`
